{%- comment -%}
  ==========================================================
  ARCHIVEOS — THE EXPANDED DECK
  RUUD BOY ARCHIVES

  The product page as an album release, not a storefront listing.

  WHAT THIS OWNS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

  This section owns *layout and presentation only*. Every
  purchasable element — price, licence tiers, add to cart — is
  rendered through Horizon's own theme blocks via
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}. Nothing about cart, variant
  resolution or checkout is reimplemented here, so the commerce
  path is exactly the one Horizon ships and tests.

  Licence tiers ARE product variants. The variant-picker block is
  placed inside .archive-deck__licence and restyled by
  assets/archive-deck.css into archival licence rows. If you find
  yourself writing variant logic in this file, stop — it belongs
  to the block.

  THE CHAMBER (RB-002.1)

  RB-001 is the artifact. The crystal shell is the physical
  foundation; the player overlay is the authoritative presentation
  of artwork, title, producer, BPM/key/tags, waveform, time and
  transport. The Stage-1 vitrine no longer renders here — the
  display case remains a homepage instrument, and archive-vitrine.js
  null-guards [data-vitrine] so it no-ops on this page.

  WHY THIS IS NOT AN .archive-card

  The deck is an artifact *host* ([data-archive-artifact]), not a
  card. archive-card-ui.js builds its queue from .archive-card only.
  A product page carrying a single card would collapse the queue to
  one entry, and next/previous would stop working — the exact bug
  the catalogue feed was built to fix. Hosts can be auditioned and
  show active state; only cards form the queue.
  ==========================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign artifact = closest.product | default: product
  assign archive_no = artifact.metafields.custom.archive.value
  assign bpm = artifact.metafields.custom.bpm.value
  assign musical_key = artifact.metafields.custom.key.value
  assign mood = artifact.metafields.custom.mood.value
  assign artifact_type = artifact.metafields.custom.type.value
  assign duration = artifact.metafields.custom.duration.value

  assign audio = artifact.metafields.custom.audio_preview.value
  if audio == blank
    assign audio = artifact.metafields.product.audio.value
  endif
-%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
  {{ closest.product | structured_data }}
</script>

<section
  class="archive-deck archive-shell"
  data-archive-deck
  data-case-position="{{ section.settings.case_position }}"
  style="
    --deck-pad-start: {{ section.settings['padding-block-start'] | default: 64 }}px;
    --deck-pad-end: {{ section.settings['padding-block-end'] | default: 96 }}px;
  "
  {%- if audio != blank %}
    data-archive-artifact
    data-track-id="{{ artifact.id }}"
  {%- endif %}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The artifact record. Identical shape to the one on every card,
    from the same snippet — the deck and the grid hand the player
    the same object.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if audio != blank -%}
    <script
      type="application/json"
      class="archive-track-data"
      data-archive-track="{{ artifact.id }}"
    >
      {%- render 'archive-track-record', product: artifact -%}
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="archive-deck__stage">
    {%- comment -%}
      RB-002.1 — the Retrieval Chamber. RB-001 is the artifact and the
      authoritative presentation of title, producer, BPM/key/tags,
      artwork, waveform, time and transport. The Stage-1 vitrine and
      audition control are retired from this composition
      (archive-vitrine.js null-guards [data-vitrine] and no-ops on
      pages without a case); the display case remains a homepage
      instrument. The Stage-1 preview toggle is retired with it —
      RB-001 formally supersedes the vitrine stage.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="archive-deck__designation">
      {%- if archive_no != blank -%}ARCHIVE {{ archive_no }} &middot; {% endif -%}RB-001 PRESERVATION CHAMBER
    </p>

    <div class="rb001-chamber" data-rb001-chamber>
      {% render 'rb001-player' %}

      {%- comment -%}
        RB-002.3R — the crystal IS the acquisition surface. On ACQUIRE
        LICENSE the chamber expands and the terms render inside the
        newly opened glass. The glass continuation is built from
        slices of the deployed CP5 shell itself (field + edge caps),
        so the expanded chamber remains one continuous crystal; the
        shell asset and every rb001 file are untouched.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rb001-chamber__extension" id="terms-of-retrieval" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="rb001-chamber__glass" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="rb001-chamber__glass-field"
               style="background-image: url('{{ 'rb001-ext-field-h.png' | asset_url }}');"></div>
          <div class="rb001-chamber__glass-edge"
               style="background-image: url('{{ 'rb001-ext-edge-r.png' | asset_url }}');"></div>
          <div class="rb001-chamber__glass-field--v"
               style="background-image: url('{{ 'rb001-ext-field-v.png' | asset_url }}');"></div>
          <div class="rb001-chamber__glass-edge--b"
               style="background-image: url('{{ 'rb001-ext-edge-b.png' | asset_url }}');"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="rb001-chamber__interior">
          <div class="archive-deck__licence">
            <h2 class="archive-deck__licence-heading">Terms of Retrieval</h2>

            {% content_for 'blocks' %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    RB-002.4 — ARCHIVE INDEX. The SELECT stage of the Retrieval
    Chamber: an archival rail beneath the chamber, backed by the same
    data the catalogue feed uses (archive-track-record per product,
    audio-bearing artifacts only — membership identical to the feed).
    Every entry is a real .archive-card in the existing bus contract:
    data-track-id + .archive-track-data + [data-archive-play], so
    archive-card-ui.js gives selection, seating, is-active/is-playing
    state and queue order for free — visible cards outrank the feed,
    so the rail IS the deck's queue, in this exact order. One engine,
    no new playback system. The Horizon product-recommendations
    section this supersedes is retired from view in archive-deck.css
    (the template JSON is deliberately not touched).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="archive-index" aria-label="Archive index">
    <h2 class="archive-index__head">Archive Index</h2>

    <ol class="archive-index__rail" role="list">
      {%- for item in collections.all.products limit: 50 -%}
        {%- capture archive_index_record -%}
          {%- render 'archive-track-record', product: item -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- assign archive_index_record = archive_index_record | strip -%}

        {%- if archive_index_record != blank -%}
          {%- assign item_no = item.metafields.custom.archive.value -%}
          {%- assign item_bpm = item.metafields.custom.bpm.value -%}
          {%- assign item_key = item.metafields.custom.key.value -%}
          {%- assign item_type = item.metafields.custom.type.value -%}

          <li class="archive-card archive-index__entry" data-track-id="{{ item.id }}">
            <script
              type="application/json"
              class="archive-track-data"
              data-archive-track="{{ item.id }}"
            >{{ archive_index_record }}</script>

            <button
              type="button"
              class="archive-index__main"
              data-archive-play
              aria-label="Audition {{ item.title | escape }}"
            >
              <span class="archive-index__no">{% if item_no != blank %}{{ item_no }}{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</span>

              {%- if item.featured_image -%}
                <img
                  class="archive-index__art"
                  src="{{ item.featured_image | image_url: width: 120 }}"
                  width="60"
                  height="60"
                  alt=""
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                >
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="archive-index__art archive-index__art--void" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              {%- endif -%}

              <span class="archive-index__title">{{ item.title }}</span>

              {%- comment -%}
                RB-002.4.1 — accession-register columns. Every field
                renders its cell in every row; a missing value keeps
                its column as an em-dash rather than letting the row
                re-flow. Alignment is the register's integrity.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="archive-index__bpm">{% if item_bpm != blank %}{{ item_bpm }} BPM{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</span>
              <span class="archive-index__key">{% if item_key != blank %}{{ item_key }}{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</span>
              <span class="archive-index__type">{% if item_type != blank %}{{ item_type }}{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</span>

              <span class="archive-index__state" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>

            <a
              class="archive-index__open"
              href="{{ item.url }}"
              aria-label="Open {{ item.title | escape }} in the archive"
            >&#8599;</a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <div class="archive-deck__panel">
    {%- comment -%}
      RB-002.1 — the duplicate identity presentation (catalog line,
      display title, spec sheet) is removed; RB-001 carries all of it
      visually. The h1 remains for document semantics only.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ artifact.title }}</h1>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  /* RB-002.3 — ACQUIRE LICENSE reveals the Terms of Retrieval.
     Deck-owned progressive enhancement; rb001-ui.js is untouched.
     The player rewrites the CTA href on trackchange, so the
     same-page test runs at click time against the current href:
     the displayed artifact's own page scrolls to terms, any other
     artifact navigates to its page as before. */
  (function () {
    document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var cta = e.target.closest('[data-rb001-acquire]');
      if (!cta || cta.tagName !== 'A' || !cta.href) return;
      var panel = document.getElementById('terms-of-retrieval');
      if (!panel) return;
      var here = location.pathname.replace(/\/+$/, '');
      var there;
      try { there = new URL(cta.href, location.origin).pathname.replace(/\/+$/, ''); }
      catch (err) { return; }
      if (here !== there) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      var chamber = cta.closest('[data-rb001-chamber]') || document.querySelector('[data-rb001-chamber]');
      if (!chamber) return;
      var open = chamber.classList.toggle('is-expanded');
      panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', open ? 'false' : 'true');
      cta.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
      if (open) {
        var reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        if (!reduced) panel.addEventListener('transitionend', function f() {
          panel.removeEventListener('transitionend', f); panel.focus({ preventScroll: true });
        });
        else panel.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      }
    });
  })();

  /* RB-002.5 — the dock as field monitor. The global player is
     continuity, not competition: on chamber pages it stands down
     while RB-001 is on stage and returns when the visitor scrolls
     past it. Presentation-only — the engine, bus and dock markup
     are untouched; archive-deck.css holds the one rule this class
     drives. */
  (function () {
    var chamber = document.querySelector('[data-rb001-chamber]');
    if (!chamber || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) return;
    var set = function (onstage) {
      document.body.classList.toggle('rb001-chamber-onstage', onstage);
    };
    var r = chamber.getBoundingClientRect();
    set(r.bottom > 0 && r.top < window.innerHeight);
    new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      set(entries[0].isIntersecting);
    }, { threshold: 0 }).observe(chamber);
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Expanded deck",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-archive-deck",
  "blocks": [{ "type": "@theme" }, { "type": "@app" }],
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "case_position",
      "label": "Display case position",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right" }
      ],
      "default": "left"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 96
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Expanded deck" }]
}
{% endschema %}
